#
# The Linux leaf drivers whose ids the hardware bus matches (one per line):
#
#   <lxsrv class> <path under third_party/linux>
#
# tools/lx_device_table.py reads each file's MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE and
# crates/drivers/hwbus/build.rs turns the ids into the Linux match table. A
# class server (lxsrv-<class>) is launched only when one of its ids matched a
# device the bus admitted. Every listed file must be in the sparse set of
# tools/third_party_fetch.sh (linux): in a checked-out tree a missing one fails the build.
#
# Only a leaf the bus matches belongs here. Of the slices that follow
# (Documentation/design/lx-driver-slices.md): the ext4 slice is chosen by
# Kconfig (LX_FS_EXT4_RO), not by a device id; the HID leaves of the URB
# adapter match on usb and hid ids, which are not a hwbus bus kind yet
# (lx_device_table.py skips them), so their lines come with the change that
# adds that kind.

# The sensor pilot: Sony IMX219 (Raspberry Pi camera v2), of id sony,imx219,
# over the native CSI-2 receiver.
media drivers/media/i2c/imx219.c
